    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d907">

                <pb facs="0714" n="598" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg598"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/13196.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Vice Consul Silliman to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-09-16">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 16, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In company with the Brazilian Minister, Mr. Long and Mr. Belt, at two o’clock
                    this afternoon I complied with the Department’s instruction to say to General
                    Carranza that the President is arranging to withdraw the American troops from
                    Vera Cruz. The message gave the greatest satisfaction. Suitable reply is being
                    prepared.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Silliman</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
